// 02_add_count.bund — Cluster-aware insert + count.
//
// Builds an observability record as a Map and inserts it via cls.add.
// In cluster mode, the record lands locally and is replicated to
// `replication_factor - 1` random Alive peers (with hint-on-failure).
// Then `cls.count` returns the cluster-wide row count.
//
// Map construction in Bund: push the empty map, then alternating
// (key_string, value) pairs, calling `set` after each pair.  `set`
// pulls (top→bottom) the value, the key, the map; pushes the updated
// map back.

// ── build the doc Map ───────────────────────────────────────────────
dict
"key"       "cpu.user"            set
"timestamp" 1700000000            set
"data"      "from cluster demo"   set

// ── insert it (returns the new UUID as a string on the stack) ──────
cls.add

// ── count rows across the cluster ──────────────────────────────────
// Empty Map → "every shard ever".  cls.count merges by summing
// per-peer `count` fields (overcounts replicated rows by ~RF).
dict cls.count

// ── echo the meta of the most-recent cluster call to the workbench ─
?cluster.meta.
